# Technical summary — poi-intelligence-ranking

> Generated from `docs/TECHNICAL_SUMMARY.md.tmpl`; every number resolves from `results/metrics.json`. The brief's "concise technical document", in the brief's order. Depth: [TECHNICAL.md](TECHNICAL.md) (thorough), [RESULTS.md](RESULTS.md) (every measurement), [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) (requirement-by-requirement coverage). All data is synthetic.

## In five lines

1. **Ranking quality** (unbiased holdout, {{meta.n_holdout_trips}} trips): raw-ranker NDCG@10 {{systems.lambdamart_ips.metrics.ndcg@10.mean|.4f}}; served top-10 (after gate, utility, MMR) {{l_holdout_report.selected_config.served_ndcg10_mean|.4f}}; content cosine {{systems.content_cosine.metrics.ndcg@10.mean|.4f}}; popularity {{systems.popularity.metrics.ndcg@10.mean|.4f}}.
2. **A train/serve skew was found and fixed:** train features saw each trip's own labelled session (median {{h_experiments.feature_skew_pre_fix.train_trips.days_since_last_interaction_median|.0f}} days since last interaction on train trips, {{h_experiments.feature_skew_pre_fix.holdout_trips.days_since_last_interaction_median|.0f}} on holdout); the first tag's "ranker no better than cosine" ({{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.ndcg10_primary|.4f}} vs {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.ndcg10_content_cosine|.4f}}) is retracted.
3. **A stated touristiness preference now steers the ranking:** served flip-overlap for trips with history {{l_holdout_report.shipped_config.flip_overlap_with_history|.3f}} → {{l_holdout_report.selected_config.flip_overlap_with_history|.3f}}; scenario-4 overlap {{l_pre_scenarios.diagnostic_vs_base_jaccard|.3f}} → {{scenarios.overlap_matrix.diagnostic_vs_base_jaccard|.3f}}.
4. **Constraints:** {{constraint_compatibility.n_hard_constraint_violations}} hard-constraint violations in {{constraint_compatibility.n_recommended}} recommended slots, against {{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.brief_additive_violations}} under the brief's additive formula.
5. **Oracle-free selection:** every choice was made on a train-carved validation split under a rule written beforehand; the true-utility oracle only scored results; the holdout was read once per decision.

## 1. Problem formulation

Given a traveler, a trip and a POI catalog, return a ranked, weighted list a downstream itinerary planner can consume. The problem is two-factor: a POI must be *preferred* and *compatible* with the trip (budget, hours, accessibility, party, mobility, reservation lead time). Two further concerns are first-class. **Exposure bias:** logged interactions record what a policy showed, so a popularity policy flatters a popularity ranker (popularity moves {{bias_gap.popularity.gap|+.4f}} NDCG@10 between the biased and unbiased holdouts, the primary model {{bias_gap.lambdamart_ips.gap|+.4f}}). **The commercial objective:** local and long-tail discovery for inbound travelers, not raw NDCG. The learning target is a graded relevance label per (trip, POI).
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §1](TECHNICAL.md#1-problem-formulation).

## 2. Architecture

Datagen (firewalled) → data preparation → POI, traveler and pair features → candidate generation (a learned full-catalog retriever at K={{e4_k_sweep.shipped_k}}, a long-tail hard floor, an interest channel) → LambdaMART ranker (IPS-weighted) → isotonic calibration → hard gate and six compatibility terms → utility → MMR re-rank → grouped-TreeSHAP explanations → ranked, weighted JSON with scores, compatibility, confidence and planner weights. The diagram and module map are in the README.
Depth: [README architecture](../README.md#architecture), [TECHNICAL.md §1](TECHNICAL.md#1-problem-formulation).

## 3. Data assumptions

Everything is synthetic: {{touristiness_axis.a_preference_distribution.n_travelers}} travelers, {{coverage.primary_system.n_catalog_pois}} catalog POIs in three destinations, inbound-traveler personas. The dataset is non-circular by construction: a latent-utility simulator whose truth lives only in `_oracle/`, readable solely by the evaluation oracle (tests scan for it). Two exposure logs: a popularity-biased training log with logged propensities, and a uniform-random holdout. Catalog dirtiness (duplicates, inconsistent categories, missing values) is injected. The simulator-quality gate passed ({{gate_dgp.n_passed}} of {{gate_dgp.n_total}} checks) and was frozen before any model work. Read every number as a property of this simulator, not of real traffic.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §0](TECHNICAL.md#0-what-the-simulator-does-and-does-not-license), [§2](TECHNICAL.md#2-dgp--circularity-defense).

## 4. Feature engineering

POI side: shrunk rating, review count, within-destination popularity percentile, a localness index, price, duration, opening hours, H3 geography, behavioural aggregates and a TF-IDF→SVD text embedding (out-of-fold R² to the latent semantics {{representation.d11_text_only.ridge_r2_oof|.3f}}). Traveler side: an explicit block (interests, budget, party, mobility, stated touristiness preference) and an implicit block (an as-of-trip taste vector in the POI embedding space plus history summaries). Pair and cross features (taste cosine, price gap, localness × touristiness) join them; {{touristiness_axis.b_training_frame_and_booster.n_booster_features}} columns reach the ranker. Every implicit feature is as-of the trip's own session start, which is the skew fix. Dropping the raw implicit-taste block changes holdout NDCG@10 by {{ablations.6.delta_ndcg@10|+.4f}}; it was not applied, because choosing it on the holdout would be selection on the holdout.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §3](TECHNICAL.md#3-feature-architecture), [§3.1](TECHNICAL.md#31-how-explicit-and-implicit-signals-are-combined-brief-section-8--measured-for-trips-with-history-the-implicit-side-wins).

## 5. Model selection

LightGBM LambdaRank, one query group per trip. The brief prefers a simple model with thoughtful features to complexity, and a two-tower ranker was measured against it: {{decision_register.rows.1.results.curve.3.two_tower.mean|.4f}} against {{decision_register.rows.1.results.curve.3.lambdamart_ips.mean|.4f}} at full training data, with no crossover on the measured range. Pointwise objectives score higher on the holdout (binary {{decision_register.rows.2.results.binary.mean|.4f}}, regression {{decision_register.rows.2.results.regression.mean|.4f}}, against {{decision_register.rows.2.results.lambdarank.mean|.4f}}); the objective was not switched because the validation-only sweep's best configuration beat the shipped one by {{derived.ranker_sweep_margin.winner_minus_shipped|.4f}}, under the pre-registered bar of {{derived.ranker_sweep_margin.adoption_bar|.3f}}.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §5](TECHNICAL.md#5-ranking-model-choice--lambdamart-justified-over-a-two-tower-ranker).

## 6. Training methodology

Train trips only. The label is the strongest interaction in a trip (view and dismiss lowest, click, then navigate, save and share, then visit and booking). Inverse-exposure-propensity weights, clipped and normalised per trip, correct the popularity-biased log. A share of training rows has its behavioural block masked so the ranker has seen the no-history regime. Early stopping uses train-carved validation trips; seed 42 throughout. Explicit cross features and a smaller tree were adopted under a pre-registered validation bar; on the holdout they added {{derived.h_holdout_effect.gain|+.4f}} NDCG@10, so essentially all of the gain over cosine comes from fixing the skew.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §5.1](TECHNICAL.md#51-a-feature-skew-bug-found-late-and-its-fix), [§5.2](TECHNICAL.md#52-explicit-cross-features-and-ranker-tuning-experiment-h), [§6](TECHNICAL.md#6-ips-correction).

## 7. Ranking methodology

Candidates first, then the ranker over a few hundred per trip. Candidate recall of exposed holdout positives is {{candidate_recall.overall.recall_mean|.3f}} overall and {{candidate_recall.long_tail.recall_mean|.3f}} in the long-tail stratum, from a hard long-tail floor that the learned retriever cannot displace: the answer to "how do you avoid eliminating long-tail POIs". The retrieval design was decided on validation with the ranker retrained per design: learned retriever {{l3b_designs.designs.A.v_ndcg10|.4f}}, legacy six-channel union {{l3b_designs.designs.B.v_ndcg10|.4f}} (long-tail recall {{l3b_designs.designs.B.long_tail_recall|.3f}}, below the brief's requirement), their union {{l3b_designs.designs.C.v_ndcg10|.4f}} ({{l3b_designs.designs.C.effective_k|.0f}} candidates, over the serving budget).
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §4](TECHNICAL.md#4-candidate-generation), [§5](TECHNICAL.md#5-ranking-model-choice--lambdamart-justified-over-a-two-tower-ranker).

## 8. Scoring methodology

`utility = hard_gate × relevance^α × compatibility^β × pref_align^γ`. Relevance is the calibrated ranker score (ECE {{calibration.ece_before|.3f}} → {{calibration.ece_after|.3f}}). Compatibility is the geometric mean of six terms; the hard gate removes POIs that are closed for the whole trip, inaccessible or unreachable. The multiplicative form deviates from the brief's additive example on purpose: a high relevance cannot outvote a failed constraint. `pref_align` is the stated touristiness preference as a per-trip factor in the scoring layer, where the brief puts trip context; γ and the MMR λ were selected together on validation. Each returned POI carries a calibrated confidence, a planner weight and a deterministic template explanation from grouped TreeSHAP.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §7](TECHNICAL.md#7-scoring-layer--multiplicative-utility-over-the-briefs-additive-formula), [§8](TECHNICAL.md#8-calibration).

## 9. Evaluation

Precision, recall and NDCG at K on the unbiased random-exposure holdout with {{meta.bootstrap_n_resamples|d}}-resample trip bootstrap CIs and paired Wilcoxon tests: the ranker beats content cosine (p={{wilcoxon.lambdamart_ips_vs_content_cosine.p_value|.2g}}; above cosine in {{~seed_vs_cosine}}). All six brief dimensions are measured: personalization, coverage, long-tail discovery, constraint compatibility, diversity, calibration. Success criteria were stated before measurement: eight met, six missed, each miss diagnosed with a measured mechanism. Some targets were set a priori without reference to the data's baselines (long-tail precision {{longtail.precision|.3f}} against 0.40, where the pool's own rate is {{derived.longtail_lift_over_base_rate.base_rate|.3f}}); they were reported as misses, not relaxed.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §10](TECHNICAL.md#10-evaluation-methodology), [RESULTS.md](RESULTS.md).

## 10. Cold-start strategy

One mechanism for all three cases: history-dependent features are as-of-trip and absent when there is no history, and the ranker is trained with the behavioural block masked. **New traveler:** NDCG@10 {{cold_start.ndcg@10_by_interaction_count_bucket.0.mean|.3f}} on {{cold_start.ndcg@10_by_interaction_count_bucket.0.n_trips_in_bucket}} no-history trips against {{cold_start.ndcg@10_by_interaction_count_bucket.>10.mean|.3f}} with a long history. **New POI:** text, structured and geo features carry it. **New destination:** no feature is destination-specific; leave-one-destination-out NDCG@10 {{lodo.per_destination.0.ndcg@10_lodo.mean|.3f}} / {{lodo.per_destination.1.ndcg@10_lodo.mean|.3f}} / {{lodo.per_destination.2.ndcg@10_lodo.mean|.3f}} against {{lodo.per_destination.0.ndcg@10_full_training.mean|.3f}} / {{lodo.per_destination.1.ndcg@10_full_training.mean|.3f}} / {{lodo.per_destination.2.ndcg@10_full_training.mean|.3f}} with the destination in training.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §10.3](TECHNICAL.md#103-cold-start-brief-section-15).

## 11. Production considerations

Prose only. At scale the retriever becomes an ANN stage over H3 shards while the ranker still scores a few hundred candidates (the ANN benchmark was not run, so this is reasoning). Offline nightly: embeddings, popularity percentiles, localness. Online: distance from the stay, open-now, availability, session context; one shared transformation library prevents train/serve skew. Weekly retrain with daily behavioural refresh, promoted on a fresh uniform-exposure slice plus interleaving. Log propensities and reserve uniform traffic as the feedback loop. Monitor feature drift, calibration, coverage, long-tail share, constraint violations (must stay zero) and cold-start share.
Depth: [TECHNICAL.md §11](TECHNICAL.md#11-production-considerations).

## Known limitations

- {{systems.lambdamart_ips.pct_of_ceiling_ndcg10|.1%}} of the oracle ceiling, against a 70% target: the taste estimator is the weak link.
- The preference factor overshoots: the served ordering follows the stated preference about {{l_holdout_report.selected_config.gradient_reproduction_of_utility.with_history.score_over_label|.0f}}x more steeply than observed behaviour.
- Confidence is weakly informative: decile Spearman {{confidence_decile_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}}.
- The new-POI dropout benefit is not demonstrated (p={{new_poi_cohort.wilcoxon_with_vs_without_dropout.p_value|.2f}}).
- Diversity sits on its constraint floor (entropy {{l_holdout_report.selected_config.category_entropy_bits|.2f}} bits) and MMR is effectively off (λ={{longtail_stages.lambda_default}}).
- The shipped LambdaRank objective is below binary and regression on the holdout ({{derived.dr3_binary_minus_lambdarank|+.4f}}); not switched, because validation did not clear the pre-registered bar.
